# Cloudflare Pages routing.
# / (index.html)  = public marketing page. It forwards any auth-callback hash/query
#                   (magic links, invites, ?join=) to /portal.html.
# /portal.html    = the portal app (login + client/team dashboards).
# Any path that is not a real static file falls back to the PORTAL (HTTP 200, no
# redirect) so client-side routes and magic-link callbacks resolve instead of 404ing
# with Cloudflare's "nothing here yet" page.
#
# NOTE: this is the correct rule for Cloudflare *Pages* (`wrangler pages deploy`).
# It is safe now because the Workers deploy path (`wrangler deploy` / wrangler.jsonc)
# was removed — that path rejected this rule as an infinite loop (error 100324).
/*    /portal.html    200
